## Always

- Practice strict Red/Green TDD on behavior changes (see `~/.claude/skills/<tdd-skill>/SKILL.md`)
- Branch from clean `main`; commit on a feature branch
- Run tests after non-trivial changes
- Invoke `multi-role-review` before merging anything cross-functional

## Never

- Commit directly to `main`
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`)
- Force-push without explicit ask
- Add files outside the repo conventions (see `AGENTS.md`)
- Touch `.env`, secrets, or credential files
- Run destructive git ops without confirmation

## When the user says

- **"Ship it"** — commit on the feature branch, push, open PR. Do not merge.
- **"Quick fix"** — single small change, skip the multi-role review.
- **"Plan it"** — produce a plan in `.claude/plans/`, do not implement until approved.
- **"Review this"** — invoke `multi-role-review` with relevant roles.

